@host = https://localhost:7202
# Development skips signature verification (Descope:Enabled=false) so these can be called directly.
# In other environments, Descope signs these calls and DescopeSignatureMiddleware verifies the HMAC.

### JIT verify — legacy user's first login (mock accepts these dev credentials)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/descope/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "legacy.user@example.com",
  "password": "Legacy#123"
}

### JIT verify — wrong credentials → 401
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/descope/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "legacy.user@example.com",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### Sync a Descope-registered user (idempotent upsert)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/descope/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "descopeUserId": "U2abc123",
  "email": "jane.roe@gmail.com",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Roe",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-15",
  "zipCode": "12345",
  "contactNumber": "123-456-7890"
}

### Health
GET {{host}}/health
